    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a more comprehensive version, also testing the other variants (which are fine):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TransferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousLinearEquiv</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- dummy doc-string -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toHomeomorph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isOpen_preimage</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv_coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousLinearEquiv</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Given a continuous additive equivalence `e : α ≃ₜ+ β`, if `β` is a topological additive group,</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">then so is `α`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMulEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTopologicalGroup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_inv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Given a continuous linear equivalence `e : α ≃L[R] β`, if `β` is a topological additive group,</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">then so is `α`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">correct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTopologicalAddGroup</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- a plain definition: the defLemma linter fires, but also a new linter about adding reducibility attributes</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: Definition `linted` of class type must be marked with `@[reducible]` or `@[implicit_reducible]`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- dummy doc-string  -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTopologicalAddGroup</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: -- Found 1 error in 6 declarations (plus 1 automatically generated ones) in the current file with 16 linters</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/- The `defLemma` linter reports:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">INCORRECT DEF/LEMMA: -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">linted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> is a def, should be lemma/theorem -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">lint</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- TODO linter bug: making the above an @[implicit_reducible] def does not lint,</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- making it a plain def does. making a lemma is correct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- A reducible def is also linted correctly.</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- dummy doc-string  -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linted'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTopologicalAddGroup</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- let's follow the linter's advice: this will silence the defLemma linter :-(</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- An implicit_reducible def is not linter any more :-/</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- dummy doc-string  -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unlinted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toContinuousAddEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTopologicalAddGroup</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: -- Found 2 errors in 8 declarations (plus 1 automatically generated ones) in the current file with 16 linters</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/- The `defLemma` linter reports:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">INCORRECT DEF/LEMMA: -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">linted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> is a def, should be lemma/theorem -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">linted'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> is a def, should be lemma/theorem -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">lint</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580732467,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1774034873
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems like <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blame/77a5160a74772214ef37caba2847cfe9ab600285/Batteries/Tactic/Lint/Misc.lean#L120\"><code>isGlobalInstance</code> was replaced with <code>isImplicitReducible</code> in a recent bump pr</a>; I'm guessing it should just be <code>isInstance</code>?</p>",
        "id": 580734110,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774035555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, it seems like <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blame/77d10578945b31d794214a66937b75a6d4311674/Batteries/Tactic/Lint/Misc.lean#L120\">a week prior to that</a>, it was changed in a bump PR from <code>isGlobalInstance</code> to <code>isInstanceReducible</code>, then to <code>isImplicitReducible</code>...</p>",
        "id": 580734640,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774035790
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the first change was probably incorrect. We just want <code>isInstance</code>.</p>",
        "id": 580734845,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774035895
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, why would we want to exempt <code>instance</code>s? <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span> Lean correctly chooses whether they should be <code>thmInfo</code>s or <code>defnInfo</code>s behind the scenes.</p>",
        "id": 580736345,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774036595
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe that used to be different when the linter was written? In that case, I'd just remove the check.</p>",
        "id": 580736525,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1774036683
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's what I'm thinking, yeah...it also checks if <code>thmInfo</code>s are <em>not</em> props, and afaik lean ensures <code>thmInfo</code>s are always props anyway (nowadays). Or maybe there's an edge case?</p>",
        "id": 580738793,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774037783
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/pull/1727\">batteries#1727</a></p>",
        "id": 580740680,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774038748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also take this chance to remove workarounds to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/2575\">lean4#2575</a> now that it's been fixed, both in <code>defLemma</code> and other linters</p>",
        "id": 580740815,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774038820
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, the automatic Mathlib CI for that PR is hitting \"uncaught exception: leantar not found in Lean sysroot. This toolchain may predate nightly-2026-03-09\"</p>",
        "id": 580741843,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774039366
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh interesting, is this a bug? It seems that the deriving handler for <code>def</code>s specifically inserts <code>@[implicit_reducible] def</code> even when the instance is Prop-typed:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: @[implicit_reducible] def instNonemptyFoo.{u_1} : ∀ (α : Type u_1), Nonempty (Foo α) :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instNonemptyFoo</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I still haven't familiarized myself with the new <code>@[implicit_reducible]</code> expectations, so I'm not sure if this is necessary even for Prop-typed instances.</p>",
        "id": 583877511,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1775513560
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I think this is a bug...the delta-deriving handler doesn't take the same pains an ordinary <code>instance</code> does to case on the prop-ness of the type.</p>",
        "id": 583879383,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1775514622
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13295\">lean4#13295</a></p>",
        "id": 583905699,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1775532489
    }
]